// textbook proof, named in `proofName`; further proofs in `alternativeProofs`; `fromDefinitions: true` marks a proof
// that uses only definitions and axioms (calculation in ℝ counts as using axioms), `foundation: true` a proof that
// rests on theory outside these graphs (named in `proof`). `area` is the three-character MSC class, as in
// data/concepts.js. `concepts` are ids of data/concepts.js or carry the prefix of another folder.
// References to theorems of other folders: "geo:" (separation theorems), "ana:" (extreme value theorem, implicit
// function theorem, Taylor, projection theorem, argument principle), "top:" (Brouwer, Banach fixed-point theorem,
// Heine–Borel), "co:" (Berge's lemma, handshaking lemma, Euler–Hierholzer, matroid basis exchange, Möbius inversion),
// and the folders built at the same time: "la:" (Cramer's rule, Cayley–Hamilton, Jordan normal form, row rank equals
// column rank), "ds:" (Lyapunov's stability theorem) and "cs:" (Cook–Levin theorem, Edmonds' blossom algorithm; the
// Christofides–Serdyukov algorithm is "cs:christofides-algorithm").
